---
/**
 * Shown by the player script when the page is served over https:// from a public host. A plain
 * ws:// socket to a LAN Music Assistant is blocked there (mixed content, and Chrome's Local Network
 * Access rule), so the player switches to the remote route: WebRTC through Music Assistant's own
 * remote access. The note tells the user what that needs.
 *
 * Dismissing it sets a cookie (see src/scripts/player.ts), so it stays gone on later visits.
 *
 * Keep inline tags on the same line as the word before them: Astro's HTML compression drops a
 * newline that sits between text and a tag, which glues the two words together.
 */
---
<div class="route-note" data-https-warning hidden>
  <p>
    This page is served over HTTPS from a public host, so the browser will not open a plain <code>ws://</code>
    socket to a Music Assistant on your network. The player therefore connects the way the Music Assistant app
    does from outside the home: over WebRTC through <strong>Music Assistant remote access</strong>. In Music
    Assistant open <em>Settings → Remote access</em>, enable it, and paste the <strong>Remote ID</strong> shown
    there into the field above; no Home Assistant Cloud subscription is needed (it only adds TURN relays for
    awkward networks). Prefer the direct <code>ws://</code> route? Serve the site from a LAN address
    (<code>npm run dev</code>, or <code>dist/</code> on a LAN http host).{' '}
    <a data-http-link href="#" hidden>Try the http:// address of this page</a>.
  </p>
  <button class="dismiss" data-control="dismiss-note" aria-label="Dismiss this note" title="Dismiss">✕</button>
</div>

<style>
  .route-note { display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; background: #2a3a55; color: #fff; padding: 10px var(--gutter); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .route-note p { margin: 0; flex: 1; }
  .route-note a { color: #fff; font-weight: 600; }
  .route-note code { background: #fff2; padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 4px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .dismiss { flex: none; padding: 2px 8px; background: #fff2; border-color: #fff4; line-height: 1.4; }

  @media (max-width: 760px) { .route-note { font-size: 13px; } }
</style>
